    "vernacular": "A 2,325 m plateau city whose centre was largely built 1935-41 by Italian planners: 2-4 storey Art Deco, Rationalist, Futurist and Novecento blocks in pastel stucco (ochre, peach, cream, pale green) with ribbon windows, curved corners, flat roofs and cantilevered canopies, laid out on a grid of palm-lined avenues (Harnet Avenue). Outer districts have low single-storey houses of render or stone with flat or corrugated-iron roofs, and Medeber is a district of tin-roofed metalworking stalls.",
