    "ornament": "Modernist Italian vocabulary: curved corner facades, horizontal ribbon windows, cantilevered concrete canopies, stepped parapets, geometric Art Deco shop signs and neon (Cinema Impero), shop awnings over arcades, black-and-white tiled floors; Orthodox churches with banded Aksumite-style stone and crosses.",
